{"TopicsController#unsubscribe dereferences tu.notification_level immediately after TopicUser.find_by(...) without a nil check, causing 500 errors when a user has no TopicUser row for that topic": 0.9690567851066589, "The unsubscribe endpoint is routed as GET but mutates TopicUser.notification_level and saves, enabling CSRF attacks where cross-site requests can toggle a logged-in user's topic notification state": 0.92470383644104, "The unsubscribe Ember route sets details.notificationReasonText to null, but notificationReasonText is a read-only computed property with no setter, causing the unsubscribe page transition to throw/assert and break": 0.1949041783809662, "The router defines a top-level topicUnsubscribe route, but the template was added as templates/topic/unsubscribe.hbs (nested route template), causing Ember to fail template resolution and render an error/blank page": 0.8792028427124023}